WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.007
In the supplied fictional package, a reader sees

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.271
red and green status marks but no written

00:00:05.329 --> 00:00:08.707
meaning or correction route. The author adds Pending,

00:00:09.253 --> 00:00:12.864
Unapproved, and Approved as text labels and explains

00:00:12.934 --> 00:00:16.045
each state. The review instructions tell a person

00:00:16.091 --> 00:00:18.796
to open the inputs and test references, check

00:00:18.854 --> 00:00:21.594
the charter, and confirm that delivery stays blocked

00:00:21.617 --> 00:00:25.791
without approval. The project author owns this tabletop

00:00:25.849 --> 00:00:28.357
design. A correction is saved in a new

00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:31.596
version and the affected paths are retested. The

00:00:31.666 --> 00:00:33.372
author checks that a reader can find the

00:00:33.442 --> 00:00:37.227
evidence and explain the unapproved state. That observation

00:00:37.285 --> 00:00:40.664
supports a specific design correction. It does not

00:00:40.722 --> 00:00:43.160
prove every access need is met or grant

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:47.417
real sending permission. For your artifact, identify actual

00:00:47.475 --> 00:00:51.191
ownership, access observations, and unresolved dependencies.
